---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { GA_ID, ADSENSE_CLIENT, REPO, CONTACT, CONTROLLER, POLICY_DATE } from "../consts";
const analytics = Boolean(GA_ID);
const ads = Boolean(ADSENSE_CLIENT);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What PhonePad collects: nothing. What this website collects, why, for how long, and your choices and rights, including under India's DPDP Act."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated {POLICY_DATE}.</p>

      <h2>The app and the companion collect nothing</h2>
      <p>
        This is worth stating first because it is the part that matters.
        PhonePad has <strong>no account system, no server, and no telemetry</strong>.
        There is nothing to sign up for, nothing to log in to, and no analytics
        in either the phone app or the Windows companion.
      </p>
      <p>
        The phone talks to your PC directly over your own network. It does not
        contact us, because no service exists behind PhonePad. You can verify
        this: the <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">entire source code is public</a>,
        and the companion never opens an outbound connection.
      </p>

      <h3>What is stored, and where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>On your phone</strong>: your layouts, your settings, and a key
          for each PC you have paired with, in the app's own storage.
          Uninstalling removes it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>On your PC</strong>: the same pairing key, the name your phone
          reports, and when it last connected, in a JSON file under
          <code>%APPDATA%\PhonePad</code>. You can delete it, and "Forget" in the
          companion removes an individual phone.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Neither is transmitted anywhere.</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>

      <h3>Who is responsible</h3>
      <p>
        PhonePad is by <strong>{CONTROLLER}</strong>, an independent software
        studio based in India, which decides what this website collects and
        why: the controller under the GDPR, and the Data Fiduciary under India's
        Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023. Contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>, or the
        <a href="/contact/">contact and grievance page</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>What is collected, and why</h3>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>What</th><th>Why</th><th>Basis</th><th>Who handles it</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>IP address and browser details, in server logs</td>
              <td>Delivering the pages and keeping the host secure</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest</td>
              <td>GitHub Pages, which hosts the site. We do not receive these logs.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Your privacy choice, in local storage</td>
              <td>Not asking you again</td>
              <td>Strictly necessary</td>
              <td>Your device only</td>
            </tr>
            {analytics && (
              <tr>
                <td>Pages viewed, referrer, device type, approximate country, a random visitor identifier</td>
                <td>Counting visits and seeing which guides help</td>
                <td>Your consent</td>
                <td>Google Analytics, on DynShift's behalf</td>
              </tr>
            )}
            {ads && (
              <tr>
                <td>Advertising identifiers in cookies, the page, approximate location</td>
                <td>Showing, measuring and protecting advertising; personalising it where allowed</td>
                <td>Your consent in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland; elsewhere legitimate interest, with the opt-outs below</td>
                <td>Google, as an independent controller</td>
              </tr>
            )}
            <tr>
              <td>Anything you post in issues or discussions</td>
              <td>Bug reports and questions</td>
              <td>Your choice to post</td>
              <td>GitHub; it is public</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Your email and message, if you write to us</td>
              <td>Answering you</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest</td>
              <td>DynShift</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {analytics && (
        <>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            Google Analytics 4 loads only after you allow it: in the EEA, the UK
            and Switzerland through Google's consent message, elsewhere through a
            two-button question from this site. Google Analytics does not store
            your IP address; it uses it to estimate your country and discards it.
            Google signals and detailed location and device data are off, and
            event data is kept for two months. See
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener nofollow"
              >how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a
            >.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      {ads && (
        <>
          <h3>Advertising</h3>
          <p>
            The documentation, troubleshooting and guide pages carry one
            advertisement each from <strong>Google AdSense</strong>, labelled
            <em>Advertisement</em>. None on the home page, the setup and download
            path, or any legal page. Google may set cookies or read similar
            identifiers to serve, measure and protect those ads, and, where you
            have allowed it, to personalise them, under
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener nofollow"
              >its own policy</a
            >. The cookies are listed on the <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a>.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2 id="your-choices">Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy settings</strong>, in the footer of every page, shows
          what applies to you and lets you change it at any time. Withdrawing
          consent is as easy as giving it.
        </li>
        {ads && (
          <li>
            <strong>EEA, UK, Switzerland</strong>: Google's consent message asks
            on your first visit, with "Consent", "Do not consent" and "Manage
            options". Nothing that needs consent is used before you answer.
          </li>
        )}
        {ads && (
          <li>
            <strong>US states with privacy laws</strong>: use
            <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</strong> in the
            footer (it appears where it applies).
          </li>
        )}
        <li>
          <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong>: if your browser sends it, this
          site treats it as an opt-out everywhere: no analytics and no
          personalised advertising.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anywhere</strong>: turn off personalised ads at
          <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener nofollow">My Ad Center</a>,
          block cookies, or use an ad blocker. Every part of the site works the same.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your privacy choice: up to 12 months in your browser, then you are asked again.</li>
        {analytics && <li>Analytics event data: 2 months at Google; only totals remain after that.</li>}
        {ads && <li>Advertising cookies: as listed on the <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a>.</li>}
        <li>Emails: deleted within 12 months of the last message unless needed for a legal claim.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who else receives data</h2>
      <p>
        Google{analytics || ads ? " (analytics and advertising)" : ""} and GitHub
        (hosting, downloads, issues). Both process data in the United States and
        elsewhere under their own safeguards for international transfers,
        including the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and the EU-US Data Privacy
        Framework. Nobody else.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Wherever you are, you can ask what DynShift holds about you and have it
        corrected or deleted: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>,
        and you will have an answer within 30 days. In practice there is very
        little: the app holds nothing of yours on our side, and this site holds
        only what is described above.
      </p>
      <h3>India (DPDP Act 2023)</h3>
      <p>
        You may ask for a summary of your personal data and its processing, and
        for its correction, completion, updating or erasure; withdraw consent
        at any time, as easily as you gave it; nominate someone to exercise your
        rights if you die or become unable to; and have a grievance answered.
        Raise it first through the <a href="/contact/">contact and grievance page</a>;
        if you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Data Protection Board
        of India. This notice is available in English or any language in the
        Eighth Schedule to the Constitution on request.
      </p>
      <h3>EEA, UK and Switzerland</h3>
      <p>
        Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, objection,
        and withdrawal of consent at any time. You may complain to your data
        protection authority.
      </p>
      <h3>United States, Brazil, Canada and elsewhere</h3>
      <p>
        DynShift does not sell personal data for money. Opt out of advertising
        "sharing" as described above. The same access, correction and deletion
        rights apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        PhonePad is not directed at children, and neither the app nor this site
        knowingly collects data from anyone under 18.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes the date above changes with it. The history is in
        <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">the repository</a>, so you can see exactly
        what changed and when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
